# RXSkyBaking native volume shape study — first art review

The baking level now uses `/Game/RXSkyBaking/Materials/MI_RXSkyBaking_ShapeStudy`.
This candidate adds regional height variation, bounded displacement, weak curl,
lower-layer wind shear, and medium-scale subtractive detail to the approved native
baseline. It remains an Unreal 5.6 legacy Volume material on a native
VolumetricCloudComponent. No external renderer or project C++ was added.

The native baseline parent and instance were read-only and their before/after
SHA256 hashes match. Original cloudsky, UltraDynamicSky and RXSkySystem assets
were not edited. The owned preview map's existing time-of-day edit was saved
before the native level switch. Cloud appearance in that preview was not updated.

The accepted SunshineClouds2 reference is
[sampleScene at a73a80b](https://github.com/Bonkahe/SunshineClouds2/blob/a73a80b08fb37b255f8f10d49debd71e5541bd70/addons/SunshineClouds2/SunshineCloudsCompute.glsl).
The separation of height, broad deformation and subtractive detail informed this
experiment. Its Godot shader, temporal reconstruction, blur and assets were not
ported. Existing owned baseline functions remain in use.

## Assets and controls

All new assets are under `/Game/RXSkyBaking`:

| Asset | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `Materials/M_RXSkyBaking_ShapeStudy` | Native volume parent; original lighting and final cleanup retained |
| `Materials/MI_RXSkyBaking_ShapeStudy` | Applied C2 art-review candidate |
| `Materials/MI_RXSkyBaking_ShapeProfile` | Same final height/region settings with curl, shear and medium carving off |
| `Textures/T_RXSkyBaking_ShapeRegions` | Generated 1024×1024 linear RGBA region data, uncompressed BGRA8 runtime data |
| `Materials/M_RXSkyBaking_ShapeRegions` | Deterministic field generator, fixed seeds |

Edit the instance's groups 10–13. Current key values:

| Parameter | Value | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Shape Enabled | 1 | 0 restores the baseline density calculation |
| Region Warp Km | 0.4 | Bounded regional expansion/compression and displacement; not an exact per-cloud scale multiplier |
| Region Clearance | 0.25 | Reduces density in generated lower-support regions |
| Height Variation | 0.8 | Regional variation of the existing vertical profile |
| Height Minimum / Maximum | 0.55 / 1.6 | Profile growth range inside the current physical shell |
| Base Height Variation | 0.08 | Interior profile shift, preserving zero/one layer endpoints |
| Curl Strength / Scale Km | 0.18 / 1.8 | Smooth asymmetry in silhouettes |
| Wind Shear Km | 0.12 | Lower-layer lateral deformation |
| Medium Shape Strength | 0.65 | Erodes existing bodies without creating new density |
| Medium Scale Km | 0.65 | Size of the additional internal lobes |
| Medium Cutoff / Softness | 0.32 / 0.3 | Carving threshold and smooth transition |
| Shape Far Preserve Start / End Km | 12 / 22 | Gradually returns to baseline shape beyond the fixed bake origin |

The component remains at 0.6 km bottom altitude and 0.7 km layer thickness.
Height Minimum/Maximum changes the internal profile, not the physical layer bounds.
For a different physical shell, edit the component and run `apply()` to synchronize
`Shape Shell Thickness Km`. `apply(save_level=True)` saves both the synchronized
owned instance and baking level. The original 15–45 km distance fade is unchanged.

The field spans 96 km about fixed world origin `(30144, -12614, 0)` cm. Its channels
are R clearance, G horizontal flow X, B height growth, A horizontal flow Y/profile.
The generator is not evaluated along view rays. It is a 1K control map, not the
final cloud bake. The volume graph adds two 2D fetches and one 3D fetch per evaluated
sample, plus arithmetic; GPU timing has not been benchmarked.

## Graph and bake contract

Shared deformed position feeds both conservative-density and extinction functions.
The same remapped normalized height feeds the profile and fragment cleanup.
Actual world position still drives the original distance fade. All baseline
scalar, vector, texture and static-switch effective values were compared and
remain unchanged, including High Frequency Noise 0.24 and the lighting controls.

Height uses an endpoint-preserving monotone remap, avoiding positive profile
density caused by cutting through an expanded shell. Medium detail only multiplies
existing extinction and runs before final fragment cleanup. With zero influence,
position, height and signed extinction pass through unchanged.

`MaterialExpressionCustom_2`, its identity/description, final extinction connection
and two scattering octaves remain intact. The bake adapter now accepts the exact
NativeBaseline or ShapeStudy parent, validates the existing final density contract,
and duplicates the actual approved parent. Shape controls, field and noise textures
follow the existing frozen parameter snapshot into transport/coverage passes.

## Verification and remaining review

- Native editor compilation and screenshots: baseline A, initial height-only B,
  initial C and tuned C2 under the same camera. Final C2 additionally inspected at
  four azimuths and the zenith. Images are in `MCPGameProject/Saved/RXSkyBaking/shape_*.png`.
- The initial B screenshot predates the final Profile instance settings; its archived
  settings are in `shape_build_report.json`. Use the current Profile instance for a
  comparison with the same C2 regional height settings.
- Current main-camera C2: `shape_C2_study.png`; wider north view: `shape_final_north.png`.
- Independent review: stronger upper lobes and underside pockets, modest overall
  improvement. No newly obvious sphere/ring silhouette, shell slicing or full-frame
  grain regression. Fine detail remains soft; detached tiny specks and some repeated
  mid/far mound shapes remain. This is an art-review candidate, not final quality.
- Numeric review: 230,625 height samples across 225 extreme combinations preserve
  finite range, exact endpoints and monotonicity; 12,960 zero-influence cases preserve
  full coordinates/height and signed extinction.
- Bake adapter: 19 mocked contract checks; live `_nodes` and parameter snapshot pass.
- Saved baking map and five new assets: hard/soft package closure is 20 owned packages,
  with no original UDS/RX/cloudsky or UnrealMCP content dependency. Editor dirty list
  was empty after saving. See `shape_validation.json`.
- Isolated project with no project Plugins folder/modules and only native Python and
  editor scripting plugins: all 20 copied assets cold-loaded; native material contract
  passed. Commandlet exit 0, 0 errors. Nine warnings concerned disabled default engine
  Oodle/ACL compression plugins, not a cloud dependency. Shader recompilation was
  requested; this is not a cook/package or isolated visual render test.
- Final Python compile, scoped whitespace check and full repository verification
  profile 42/42 passed. Full log: `shape_full_verification.log`.

No full BC7 cloud rebake or preview appearance update was performed. Baking-level
art acceptance remains the next step before the existing 1K packed bake and preview
validation. The user subsequently authorized submitting this candidate to `main`.
Final submission evidence and before/after images are archived in the adjacent
`RXSkyBaking_ShapeStudy_20260913/` directory. The final saved candidate is checked
again in isolation; it includes the synchronized shell thickness persisted by `apply()`.
